# Rowan's scenes in Maplewood. The format is described at the top of scripts/story.gd.

== rowan_away
# before the fence scene he's up on the hill with his flock
@trigger talk rowan
@requires act1_arrived !met_rowan
> He's counting sheep on the far side of the hill and doesn't look up. Maybe later.

== rowan_town_chat
# the first time you find him in Maplewood, after Act 1
@trigger talk rowan
@requires met_rowan
@once
@camera rowan 6
Rowan (neutral): You found the town, then.
Nora (wry): It found me. There's one road.
Rowan (wry): Two, if you count the one the sheep take.
? What do you say?
- Thanks again for the other day. I'd still be chasing them. -> honest | trust rowan +2; familiarity rowan +4
- I'd have managed. I always do. -> guarded | familiarity rowan +2; set nora_guarded
- Are you always this friendly? -> tease | familiarity rowan +3
@label honest
Rowan (happy): You'd have caught one. Eventually. The slow one.
Rowan (warm): Come find me on the hill if they give you trouble. They usually do.
@goto done
@label guarded
Rowan (neutral): Fair enough.
Rowan (warm): Offer stands anyway. The hill, past your fence. If you need a hand.
@goto done
@label tease
Rowan (wry): This is me at my friendliest. Ask Theo.
Nora (happy): I might.
@label done
> He tips his head and goes back to watching the road, like he's waiting for something that never comes.

# --- Romance v1: talk topics, one a day (@daily), as he warms up --------------------------------
# Order matters: the first scene whose conditions hold plays. Canon is in data/personas.json:
# Ellie first, then the long evenings, and Anna only once he trusts her.

== rowan_topic_flock
@trigger talk rowan
@requires seen_rowan_town_chat
@when hearts rowan >= 1
@once
@daily
@camera rowan 6
Rowan (wry): Bramble's been at your fence again. The one with the black ear.
Nora (surprised): They have names?
Rowan (neutral): Course they have names. Bramble, Sleet, Drizzle, Fog, Gale. And Margaret.
Nora (wry): Weather, weather, weather... Margaret?
Rowan (wry): She came with the name. You don't argue with a Margaret.
? What do you say?
- You should let me name the next one. -> name | familiarity rowan +4; set rowan_sheep_named
- I'm going to say hello to Margaret properly. -> margaret | familiarity rowan +3; trust rowan +1
@label name
Rowan (neutral): Go on, then.
Nora (happy): Purl. Because she'll be the one that does everything backwards.
Rowan (happy): ...Purl. Fine. Don't tell the others it was you.
@goto done
@label margaret
Rowan (happy): She'll ignore you. It's how she shows respect.
@label done
> He goes back to watching the hill, but the corner of his mouth stays up for a while.

== rowan_topic_ellie
@trigger talk rowan
@requires seen_rowan_topic_flock
@when trust rowan >= 5
@once
@daily
@camera between rowan nora 6
Rowan (neutral): Your gran taught me to darn socks. Sat me at her table and wouldn't let me leave till I'd done a heel.
Nora (happy): That sounds like her.
Rowan (wry): She fed me after. Bread, burnt black on the bottom. Every loaf. Twenty years and not one that wasn't.
> Something about the way he says it, like it's the best bread he's ever had.
@memory on 1.4
> Gran's kitchen. Nora is nine, and the smoke alarm is going.
Gran (happy): Don't just stand there, Norrie. Fan it. With the tea towel. No, the clean one.
Nora (happy): Gran, it's on fire!
Gran (wry): It's not on fire. It's on flavour. Cut the bottom off and nobody needs to know.
@memory off 1.4
@journal memory Gran's bread | Burnt on the bottom, every single loaf. "It's not on fire, it's on flavour." Rowan ate twenty years of it and never once complained.
? What do you tell him?
- She used to say the burnt bit was "flavour." -> share | trust rowan +3; familiarity rowan +3
- I miss her. I didn't visit enough. -> guilt | trust rowan +4; familiarity rowan +2; set nora_gran_guilt
@label share
Rowan (happy): She told me that too. I believed her for about a year.
@goto done
@label guilt
Rowan (neutral): She knew where you were. She talked about you like you'd only just gone out.
Nora (sad): That's worse, somehow.
Rowan (warm): It's not. Give it time and it's not.
@label done

== rowan_topic_evenings
@trigger talk rowan
@requires seen_rowan_topic_ellie
@when hearts rowan >= 2
@when trust rowan >= 9
@once
@daily
@camera between rowan nora 6
Rowan (neutral): Evenings get long up on the hill. Didn't used to notice.
Rowan (neutral): Your lights have been on at Birchfield. Late, some nights.
Nora (wry): Knitting. Or not sleeping. Usually both.
Rowan (warm): It's good, seeing them. Like the place is awake again.
? What do you say?
- You could come down for tea. I've got a kettle and terrible biscuits. -> tea | romance rowan +2; familiarity rowan +3
- It's nice, knowing someone's up there too. -> nice | romance rowan +1; trust rowan +2
- I'll leave one on for the sheep. -> tease | romance rowan +1; familiarity rowan +2
@label tea
Rowan (surprised): ...Terrible biscuits. You're selling it hard.
Rowan (warm): Alright. I'll bring the good ones.
@set rowan_tea_offer
@goto done
@label nice
Rowan (neutral): Yeah. It is.
> Neither of them says anything else for a while. Neither of them minds.
@goto done
@label tease
Rowan (wry): They'd like that. Margaret's afraid of the dark.
@label done

# --- The first gift that matters ------------------------------------------------------------------

== rowan_first_sweater
# plays the first time she gives him a sweater (after the usual gift stats)
@trigger gift rowan sweater
@requires met_rowan
@once
@camera between rowan nora 5
> He holds it up. Then he holds it up again, like it might have changed.
Rowan (surprised): You made this.
Nora (wry): I make a lot of them. It's sort of my whole thing now.
Rowan (neutral): Not for me, you don't.
> He doesn't put it on. He folds it, carefully, the way you'd fold a flag.
Rowan (warm): Ellie made me a hat once. I've still got it. It's got a hole you could put your fist through.
Nora (happy): Bring it round. I'll fix it.
Rowan (warm): ...I might.
@romance rowan +1
@set rowan_has_sweater

# --- The first date: the back field at sunset ----------------------------------------------------

== rowan_date_invite
@trigger talk rowan
@requires seen_rowan_topic_evenings !date1_invited !date1_not_yet
@when hearts rowan >= 3
@when romance rowan >= 3
@once
@daily
@camera between rowan nora 5
Rowan (neutral): There's a rock at the top of Ellie's back field. Best view of the valley at sunset.
Rowan (neutral): Ellie used to sit up there with a flask. Said it was the only place nobody could find her.
Nora (wry): And you're telling me where it is.
Rowan (warm): I'm telling you I'll be on it. Tonight, if the weather holds. If you want the company.
? Go up and watch the sunset with him?
- I'd like that. -> yes | romance rowan +1; set date1_invited
- Not yet. Ask me again? -> later | trust rowan +1; set date1_not_yet
@label yes
Rowan (happy): Bring a coat. It gets cold the second the sun goes.
@goal Meet Rowan on the rock in the back field at sunset | 23.4 -16.4
@home rowan 24.4 -16.0
@end
@label later
Rowan (neutral): I will. The rock's not going anywhere.

== rowan_date_invite_again
@trigger talk rowan
@requires date1_not_yet !date1_invited
@when hearts rowan >= 4
@once
@daily
@camera between rowan nora 5
Rowan (neutral): Rock's still there. So am I.
Nora (happy): Then so am I. Tonight?
Rowan (warm): Tonight.
@set date1_invited
@goal Meet Rowan on the rock in the back field at sunset | 23.4 -16.4
@home rowan 24.4 -16.0

== rowan_date1
@trigger area back_field
@requires date1_invited !date1_done
@once
@goal
@fade out 1.0
@weather clear
@if hour >= 17 -> placed
@time 18.0
@label placed
@prop rock date_rock 23.6 -16.6 0
@place nora 23.15 -16.35 10
@place rowan 24.05 -16.35 350
@anim nora SitIdle
@anim rowan SitIdle
@camera between rowan nora 4.5 low
@fade in 1.6
> The whole valley's gone gold. Down the hill the cottage is small enough to cover with a thumb.
Rowan (neutral): Told you. Best rock.
Nora (happy): Gran's rock.
Rowan (wry): Gran's rock. I just borrow it.
> Far off on the next hill, his flock drifts like dandelion seeds.
Nora (neutral): Can I ask why you stay out here? You could be anywhere.
Rowan (neutral): Could be. Nowhere else has my sheep in it.
Rowan (neutral): And it's quiet. Took me a while to like the quiet. Now I'd miss it.
Nora (neutral): Knitting's like that for me. It's just counting, with your hands. When everything else is too loud.
Rowan (warm): Is it loud? Still?
Nora (sad): Less. Today, less.
@if !rowan_has_sweater -> hat
Rowan (wry): I'm wearing your sweater, by the way. In case you hadn't noticed.
Nora (happy): I noticed.
@label hat
> He digs in his coat and pulls out a woolly hat, old and soft, with a hole you could put your fist through.
Rowan (neutral): Ellie made me this. Twelve winters ago.
Nora (warm): Give it here.
@anim nora SitKnit
> She has a needle and a little yarn in her pocket. Of course she does. It takes her four minutes.
> He watches the whole time, like she's doing a magic trick.
Rowan (surprised): ...You can't even see where it was.
Nora (warm): That's the idea. You go round the hole, not across it. Then it's part of the hat again.
@anim nora SitIdle
> The sun goes. It gets cold, exactly as promised.
? He's close enough that their shoulders nearly touch.
- Lean your head on his shoulder. -> lean | romance rowan +4; trust rowan +1; set rowan_close
- "This was nice. Same time next week?" -> week | romance rowan +2; familiarity rowan +4; set rowan_next_week
- "I'm not ready for this to be anything yet. Is that okay?" -> slow | trust rowan +4; set rowan_slow
@label lean
> She leans. He goes very still, then very carefully doesn't move at all.
Rowan (warm): ...Alright, then.
@goto end
@label week
Rowan (happy): Same rock. I'll bring a flask.
@goto end
@label slow
Rowan (warm): Sheep don't rush. Neither do I.
Nora (warm): Thank you.
Rowan (wry): Don't thank me. It's just how I'm built. Slow.
@label end
@journal note The back field | Watched the sun go down from Gran's rock with Rowan. Fixed the hat Gran knit him, round the hole, not across it.
@set date1_done
@fade out 1.4
@anim nora off
@anim rowan off
@prop_remove date_rock
@home rowan off
@time 20.0
@place nora 22.6 -15.4 160
@camera player
@fade in 1.2
@toast Rowan walks you to the edge of the field, and then home.

# --- After the date ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

== rowan_topic_anna
# canon (personas.json): he lost his wife, Anna, five years ago, to illness.
@trigger talk rowan
@requires date1_done
@when trust rowan >= 14
@once
@daily
@camera between rowan nora 5
Rowan (neutral): I told you I stopped setting the table for two. I never said why.
Rowan (sad): Anna. My wife. Five years in March. She was ill a long time, and then she wasn't, and then she was gone.
> He says it plainly, like a fact about weather, but his hands have stopped moving.
Rowan (neutral): She'd have liked you. She'd have made you knit her something ridiculous.
? What do you say?
- What would she have asked for? -> ask | trust rowan +3; romance rowan +1
- Thank you for telling me. -> thank | trust rowan +4
@label ask
Rowan (happy): Socks with sheep on. Each one a different sheep. She'd have wanted them named.
Nora (warm): I could do a Margaret.
Rowan (happy): ...You could do a Margaret.
@goto done
@label thank
Rowan (warm): Didn't plan to. It's easier, up here. With you.
@label done
@journal note Anna | Rowan's wife. Five years ago. He wanted me to know.
